T*
(1. ActivityInfo authentication) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(web-monitor will use an ActivityInfo personal API token for authenticated access. The token) Tj
T*
(will not be stored in Git or hard-coded in the application.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(For local development, Codex can configure an ignored local environment file and wire the) Tj
T*
(application to read the token from an environment variable. For deployment, the token should) Tj
T*
(be stored in Google Cloud Secret Manager and read by the App Engine service at runtime.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. ActivityInfo schema and bootstrap) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The ActivityInfo database structure should be created through the API as part of a one-time) Tj
T*
(bootstrap process rather than built manually.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The initial schema will center on:) Tj
T*
(- Monitored Sites: URL, crawl depth, allow/domain restriction, schedule, and active status.) Tj
T*
(- Crawls: timestamp, status, observed snapshot, crawl metrics, and error/change information.) Tj
T*
(- Snapshots: one record for each distinct observed state.) Tj
T*
(- Snapshot Items: child/subform records containing the extracted items used to represent a) Tj
T*
(snapshot.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Snapshot Items should be implemented as an ActivityInfo subform of Snapshot. The bootstrap) Tj
T*
(should create the parent form, add the subform field, define the child schema, and then read) Tj
T*
(the resulting schemas back to verify the relationship.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(The bootstrap should also seed roughly three to four monitored sites chosen to demonstrate) Tj
T*
(different rates of change. The initial set should favor structured, crawlable public pages) Tj
T*
(over noisy commercial news homepages. Current candidates include Python.org, Python Insider,) Tj
T*
(IMDb Top 250, and a highly stable IANA page.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Runtime execution should only read and write records; schema creation and schema changes) Tj
T*
(remain explicit bootstrap/migration operations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Query interface and reporting) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
